1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,470
When you were at school, were you ever told to stop daydreaming and concentrate?
上学时，你有没有被老师提醒过别再做白日梦、要专心听讲？

2
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:13,070
It was easy for your mind to wander if you weren’t interested in what you were learning or if you had better things to think about.
如果对正在学的内容不感兴趣，或者心里想着更有意思的事情，思绪就很容易飘走。

3
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:22,440
Staying focused can still be a challenge in adult life, but understanding how to do it, and knowing what is distracting you, can help.
即便到了成年，保持专注依旧是个难题，但只要弄明白如何集中注意力，清楚是什么在干扰自己，就能有所改善。

4
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:29,880
Scientists have looked at what makes us procrastinate and found a number of ways to help us stay in the zone.
科学家们研究了导致人们拖延的原因，并找到了不少帮助大家保持专注状态的方法。

5
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:34,030
One of the most obvious things is eliminating noise.
最显而易见的方法之一就是消除噪音。

6
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:45,120
Research by Science Focus magazine found silence is best for concentration, or a gentle background hum and coffee shop noise is great!
《科学焦点》杂志的一项研究发现，安静的环境最有利于集中注意力，而轻微的背景音或是咖啡馆里的嘈杂声也很不错。

7
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:56,680
It also found turning off notifications on your phone, or switching it off altogether, removes a major distraction and helps us focus on the task at hand.
该研究还指出，关闭手机通知，或是直接把手机关机，能消除一大干扰源，帮助我们专注于手头的任务。

8
00:00:56,680 --> 00:01:02,750
Another possible cure for a short attention span is brain training.
针对注意力持续时间短的问题，另一个可行的解决办法是大脑训练。

9
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:14,730
Psychologists and neuroscientists are increasingly interested in our ability to knuckle down and have looked at what we can change inside our head to make us concentrate.
心理学家和神经科学家对人们沉下心来做事的能力越来越感兴趣，并且一直在研究我们可以通过哪些大脑层面的调整来提升专注力。

10
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:34,390
An article for BBC Future by Caroline Williams says that “Attention Researcher Nilli Lavie of University College London has found that making a task more visually demanding… takes up more processing power and leaves the brain nothing left to process distractions.”
卡罗琳·威廉姆斯为英国广播公司未来频道撰写的一篇文章提到：“伦敦大学学院的注意力研究员妮莉·拉维发现，增加一项任务的视觉难度……会占用大脑更多的处理能力，使其没有余力去处理干扰因素。”

11
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:38,540
So, keeping your mind busy might be the answer.
如此说来，让大脑保持忙碌状态或许就是解决之道。

12
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:42,210
There are more practical tips to keeping your mind focused.
还有更多实用的小技巧能帮我们集中注意力。

13
00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:52,610
These include making a list or timetable of the tasks you have to do, finding a workspace where you’re not tempted to do other things, or chewing some gum!
比如，把要做的任务列成清单或时间表，找一个不会诱使自己分心去做别的事的工作区域，或是嚼点口香糖！

14
00:01:52,610 --> 00:01:58,860
It’s possible the movement in your mouth occupies parts of the brain that might otherwise get distracted.
口腔的咀嚼动作有可能会占用大脑中原本容易被干扰的部分。

15
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:05,220
But according to Science Focus magazine, distraction isn’t all bad.
但据《科学焦点》杂志称，分心也并非全然是坏事。

16
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:14,170
“If we were always so focused that we never got distracted, we’d miss potential changes, such as threats, in our environment.
“如果我们总是高度专注、从不分心，就会错过环境中潜在的变化，比如一些威胁。

17
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:17,140
Distraction is vital for survival.”
分心对生存而言至关重要。”
